@text 
@nl
@text A tiny document authored in the \emph{Markdown} dialect. It exercises the
@nl
@text post-\code{markup} prose transform: paragraphs and \strong{emphasis} become HTML, and the
@nl
@text fenced float directives produce numbered, labelled equations, figures, and
@nl
@text tables. The mass–energy relation is \ref{eq:mass}, sketched in
@nl
@text \ref{fig:diagram} and tabulated in \ref{tbl:units}.
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ```math \label{eq:mass}
@nl
@text E = mc^2
@nl
@text ```
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ```figure \label{fig:diagram}
@nl
@text \caption{A \emph{schematic} of $E = mc^2$.}
@nl
@text <img src="diagram.svg" alt="mass to energy">
@nl
@text ```
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ```table \label{tbl:units}
@nl
@text \caption{Symbols and their units.}
@nl
@text | Symbol | Unit |
@nl
@text |--------|------|
@nl
@text | \code{E} | J  |
@nl
@text | \code{m} | kg |
@nl
@text ```
@nl
@text 
@nl
